{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "ae-sieve — how a note finds its voice (AE Machine, manual ch. 14).",
    "",
    "Eight AE voices hear every note of `seq`; each plays only the notes that pass",
    "its sieve: fm note%4=0, modal %3=1, drone %4=2, hats %4=3, sub %5=4, string",
    "%6=5, metal %8=1, crack %7=3. Because the divisors are 3..8 the pattern of who",
    "answers repeats only after 840 notes. Learn five notes: 36 fm alone, 37 modal",
    "alone, 42 drone alone, 45 crack alone, 59 hats+sub+string+crack.",
    "",
    "Watch the lamps (lilypad) or `lastEventTime`: a voice that declines a note",
    "doesn't light.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /seq note=37,64,38,46,40,64,43,60,37,64,58,46,54,64,38,65   every note +1: a new kit",
    "  /seq note=36                     one note on every step: FM alone",
    "  /seq note=59                     four instruments at once",
    "  /hats sieve=all                  the hats answer everything",
    "  /crack sieve=4:1                 give the crack a different share",
    "  /seq shape=wide                  same notes, a different walk",
    "  /seq metrics=1/16,1/16,1/32,1/32,1/8t    irregular steps",
    "  /harmony tuning=bohlen_pierce    the quant voices (modal, drone, string) retune"
  ],
